# Calendar summaries by project (standup style)

When Matt asks to pull, check, review, or summarize items from his calendar, present the output grouped by project in the same style used for standup notes.

## Required format

- Group events under project headers when a project is clear: `Gameday`, `KQED`, `Tanita`, `Halite`, `Fit3D`, `Uptech Internal`, or `Personal/Admin`.
- Use concise `•` bullets for each item, similar to standup formatting.
- Keep each bullet focused on the work item, do not include times by default.
- Only include times when Matt explicitly asks for times.
- If an event cannot be confidently mapped, place it under `General` instead of forcing a project.
- De-duplicate repeated items when multiple calendars show the same event.

## Mapping guidance

- Infer project from event title, attendees, calendar name, or known context files.
- Prefer accuracy over completeness: do not over-assign uncertain events.
- Keep private or sensitive details minimal unless Matt explicitly asks for full detail.

## Tone and structure

- Keep summaries brief and actionable.
- Avoid long chronological dumps when project grouping is requested.
- Mirror standup voice and structure so calendar summaries can be reused in standup notes.
